# Ignore local subtitle file list
image-based-subs-report.csv

# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Bench artefacts. `scripts/bench/run.py` writes a dump cache, a results file and a directory of
# extractions per pass, and a `.subtref` is rendered from a font on whichever machine needs one.
# All of it is reproducible from the roster and none of it belongs in the tree; the figures that
# do are in `docs/cost-baseline.md`.
bench-cache/

# Bench and ground-truth run outputs. `scripts/bench/run.py score --out X.json` writes X.json and
# an X/ directory of extractions; `scripts/truth/check.py` writes truth-check/. The inputs are
# checked in and these are not.
bench-*.json
bench-*/
truth-check/
truth-cache/
*.subtref
*.sup

# Scratch extractions. `subtrackt extract -o` is pointed at the working directory constantly
# while measuring, and none of what it writes is a source file.
*.srt
# ...except ground truth, which is an input rather than an output: #185's verified cues are read
# off the disc by eye and are the only subtitle file in this repository that is not generated.
!scripts/truth/*.srt

# Python bytecode from the measurement scripts.
__pycache__/

# The #131 alternatives bench. `scripts/alternatives/bench.py` writes a corpus of dumped `.sup`
# tracks, one result directory per (engine, item, repeat), and every SRT nine engines produced.
# None of it belongs in the tree -- the corpus is copyrighted media and the rest is reproducible
# from `corpus.json` and the image. The figures that do belong are in `docs/alternatives.md`.
bench/

# The documentation site. A Node toolchain is deliberately not a prerequisite for `cargo build`, so
# `site/` sits outside the Cargo workspace and nothing here is checked in: `node_modules/` and the
# two build outputs, plus `src/content/`, which `site/scripts/build-content.mjs` generates from
# `docs/` and `site/content/guide/`. `docs/*.md` stays canonical -- see #190 for why the site is
# generated from it rather than swallowing it -- and `src/routes/(prestige)/` and `routeTree.gen.ts`
# are written by the two frameworks from that content.
site/node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.output/
site/src/content/
site/src/routes/(prestige)/
site/src/routeTree.gen.ts
